# License Header

## Guideline

- Start every new code file, including test files, with the license header below; report an existing code file that lacks it instead of adding it, unless the task covers it.
- The header comes first in the code file, followed by a blank line; only a line a tool requires at the very top (a shebang, an encoding line) stays above it.
{%- set line_comment_tokens = {
    'go': '//',
    'javascript': '//',
    'rust': '//',
    'typescript': '//',
    'powershell': '#',
    'python': '#',
    'shell': '#',
} %}
{%- set block_comment_tokens = {
    'css': ['/*', '*/'],
} %}
{%- set comment_languages = languages | select('in', line_comment_tokens) | list %}
{%- set block_comment_languages = languages | select('in', block_comment_tokens) | list %}
- The header text below is plaintext; when writing it into a code file, prefix every line with the file language's line-comment token{{ ':' if comment_languages else '.' }}
{%- for language in comment_languages %}
  - `{{ language }}`: `{{ line_comment_tokens[language] }}`
{%- endfor %}
- In a code file whose language has no line comments, wrap the header text in one block comment instead, with its opening and closing delimiters on lines of their own{{ ':' if block_comment_languages else '.' }}
{%- for language in block_comment_languages %}
  - `{{ language }}`: `{{ block_comment_tokens[language][0] }}` and `{{ block_comment_tokens[language][1] }}`
{%- endfor %}
- Documentation and data formats (e.g. Markdown, JSON, YAML, TOML) don't carry the header, even where they allow comments.
<!-- Project-specific / Guideline -->

{%- if license_header == 'Full' %}
{%- set notice_license = license|lower|replace('-or-later','')|replace('-only','') %}

## Full header

The header text for each code file is:

```
{% include 'licenses/' ~ notice_license ~ '-notice.jinja' -%}
```

